    "number": 85,
    "title": "Use the shared npm cache in setup guidance",
    "body": "Refs #84\n\n## Summary\n\n`docs/development.md` (Workflow tooling): replaces \"add `--cache /tmp/codex-nanoleaf-npm-cache`\" with guidance to use npm's default cache (`~/.npm`) and to report a read-only cache instead of redirecting it. `/tmp` can be a small RAM-backed filesystem shared by every session.\n\n## Why\n\nOn 2026-09-23 the WSL host's RAM-backed `/tmp` filled completely, partly from caches and per-task installs placed there. The Codex local-development sandbox profile now allows writes to `~/.npm`, so the workaround is no longer needed.\n\n## Candidate evidence\n\n- Base: `fad152e978e057258a9ebc8524469808107dbada` (origin/main). Head: `4c4c83bafbcb4fe2e6f20d8cf19a5d85bfe28658`. Merge-base: the base.\n- Diff: `git diff fad152e978e057258a9ebc8524469808107dbada...4c4c83bafbcb4fe2e6f20d8cf19a5d85bfe28658` (`docs/development.md` only). Worktree clean at head.\n- Validation at head: `npm ci` exit 0; `npm run check:workflow` exit 0 (14 of 14 items valid, inventory unchanged); `npm run test:workflow` exit 0 (10 of 10).\n\n## Scope notes\n\nDocumentation only; no bridge, map, installer or light behavior change, no OpenSpec change, no UI change. Related: #82 / #83 (cleanup after delivery).\n\n## Reviews\n\nIndependent Standards and Specification reviews pending.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
    "state": "open",
